# Complex (line 15) scores ~35 and must fire; Simple (line 38) is ~2 and must not.
#
# Both line numbers moved on 2026-08-10 when the DEFAULT threshold was retuned
# 15 -> 30 (measured: the median flagged routine in drag-lint's own corpus scored
# 22, so the old default flagged the median rather than the outliers). The
# fixture's Complex routine was raised from ~20 to ~35 so it still proves the
# rule FIRES; it is not the place that pins the threshold value -- that is
# DEFAULT_CYCLOMATIC_THRESHOLD in DRagLint.Lint.RuleCatalog, read by both the
# catalog and every checker call site.
cyclomatic-complexity 15
!cyclomatic-complexity 38
